WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:06.600
The next Dune movie comes out in November
– and new trailers and interviews reveal

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.950
new characters like Feyd-Rautha Harkonnen
and Princess Irulan.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.480
So who are these characters, what’s happening
in the trailer, and how does it compare to

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.570
the book?

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:21.689
This video has no big spoilers – just some
background info from the book and from interviews

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:24.590
to get us ready for Dune Part Two.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.210
So in the first Dune movie, the Atreides took
over the planet Arrakis.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.890
In the deserts of Arrakis are giant sandworms,
and a precious resource called spice.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:41.030
The Atreides were attacked and defeated by
the Harkonnens, with the help of the Emperor’s

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.030
soldiers.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:47.010
So Paul and Jessica Atreides escaped and joined
the Fremen in the desert.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:52.600
Paul had visions of the future – seeing
himself as a religious leader, unleashing

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.230
a terrible holy war.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:01:00.770
Director Denis Villeneuve says the first Dune
movie is “contemplative” – it’s slow.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:06.600
But that the next movie, Part Two, is an “action-packed,
epic war movie”.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.780
The trailer shows Paul and Chani fighting
Harkonnen soldiers.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:16.670
The trailer says ‘long live the fighters’,
which is a Fremen battle cry – this is a

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:19.180
war for control of Arrakis.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:24.610
But amidst the violence and sci fi shenanigans,
Villeneuve centres the story on the human

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.650
relationship of Paul and Chani.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:32.430
In the trailer, Paul and Chani kiss, and say
that they will stay together – which is

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.640
similar to a line in the book.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.299
Chani’s actor Zendaya says that despite
the “intense circumstances”, these are

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.940
just “two young people”, “trying to
grow up and fall in love”.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:47.600
She draws on relatable feelings of teenage
awkwardness.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:53.770
And there are awkward moments in the book
– Chani makes Paul blush, and feel embarrassed

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:54.850
when they meet.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:02:00.030
Paul and Chani are from different cultures,
they’re literally from different planets,

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.380
so they have misunderstandings, and they learn
from each other.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:10.030
In the trailer, Paul compares the sand dunes
of Arrakis to the ocean waves of his homeworld,

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.030
Caladan.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:16.569
This is based on a bit in the book, when Chani
asks about the waters of Paul’s birthworld.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:21.879
In the trailer, Paul talks about swimming
and diving in water, and Chani can’t imagine

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:25.890
that’s even possible, because water is so
rare on Arrakis.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:31.170
That’s based on a different bit from the
book, where Paul explains what drowning and

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.200
boats are to a woman.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.260
In the Dune book, we don’t get to see much
of the beginning of Paul and Chani’s relationship.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:43.180
The new movie explores their relationship
more, using bits from the book to inspire

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.620
new scenes.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:50.420
The trailer shows a soldier burning corpses
– they look like dead Atreides from the

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.300
battle in the first movie.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:57.440
Previously, Paul had visions of burning corpses,
and they were connected with his vision of

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.880
a holy war.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:04.290
Paul sees death in his future and in his past.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.120
We see a portrait of Paul’s dead father
Leto burning.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.580
In the first movie, we saw a portrait of Leto’s
father, the Old Duke.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.400
The Old Duke died when he faced a bull in
an arena and was killed.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.580
Like how Leto faced the Harkonnens on Arrakis,
and was killed.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:30.050
Now Paul is facing danger – will he be killed,
like his father and grandfather before him?

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.270
In the trailer, Jessica says Leto didn’t
believe in revenge.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.489
Leto spoke of honour, honesty, and morality.

00:03:38.489 --> 00:03:41.110
Will Paul live up to these ideals?

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:47.170
In the book, Leto says that if they compromise
their morals to survive, the honourable Atreides

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:51.270
banner “could come to mean many evil things”.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:57.470
The trailer shows Jessica in a basket with
some Fremen, as they ride on a sandworm – you

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.480
can see this guy steering the sandworm with
ropes.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.959
Cause the Fremen use sandworms to travel,
and certain important people ride worms in

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:09.040
a palanquin, this special basket.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:15.670
We see Jessica with blue eyes, which is caused
by spice – you can see spice on her nose,

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.500
like she’s been snorting it.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:22.550
We see Jessica in fancy costumes, and she
has markings on her face, similar to this

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:25.490
vision Paul had in the first movie.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:31.270
Villeneuve says these markings are tattoos,
linked with the prophecy of the Lisan al-Gaib,

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.250
the messiah who will save the Fremen.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:39.340
Some Fremen believe that Jessica and Paul
fit this prophecy, that they are the chosen

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.520
ones.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:45.680
These markings are on Jessica’s clothes
as well as her face, she is physically cloaking

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.650
herself in this prophecy, playing the role
of messiah.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:55.620
Jessica wants the Fremen to believe that she
and Paul are the chosen ones so that she can

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.710
use the Fremen to help her and Paul.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.740
And Paul doesn’t like this.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:06.350
In the trailer, Jessica says they give “hope”
to the Fremen, but Paul says “That's not

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:07.350
hope”.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:12.889
Because in the first movie we learned that
the Fremen prophecy is at least partly a lie.

00:05:12.889 --> 00:05:19.130
The Bene Gesserit planted this prophecy on
Arrakis as a tool to control the Fremen.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:26.020
Paul doesn’t want to exploit Fremen religion
– though, he does need the Fremen’s help

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.289
to survive on Arrakis.

00:05:28.289 --> 00:05:35.669
And there is some truth to the prophecy – Paul
does have real power to see the future.

00:05:35.669 --> 00:05:41.300
Jessica believes that Paul may be the Kwisatz
Haderach, a superhuman created by the Bene

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.300
Gesserit breeding program.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:50.020
So.. it’s complicated – Paul and Jessica
are playing with powerful dangerous forces

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:57.139
of religion, politics, visions and predictions,
and Paul knows this could lead to terrible

00:05:57.139 --> 00:05:58.699
destruction.

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:04.750
We see a new character, played by Florence
Pugh – this is Princess Irulan Corrino.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:10.020
Irulan is the daughter of the Emperor of the
Universe, Shaddam Corrino.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:14.410
We haven’t seen the Emperor yet, but he’ll
be played by Christopher Walken.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:20.880
Irulan is described in the book as tall blonde
and beautiful, confident, and intelligent.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:27.490
Irulan has been trained by the Bene Gesserit
– so she has powers of perception, control,

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.930
and combat.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:34.639
In the Dune book, each chapter starts with
a quote from a book written by Irulan.

00:06:34.639 --> 00:06:40.840
Irulan writes about history, and philosophy,
giving us worldbuilding details and thematic

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.790
ideas for each chapter.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.220
Irulan also writes about her own life.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:52.250
As the Emperor’s daughter, Irulan had a..
difficult childhood – she writes “A Royal

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:59.069
Family is not like other families” – in
her home, political plots and intrigues were

00:06:59.069 --> 00:07:05.190
“constant and oppressive”, and even her
own father was a potential threat to her.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:09.000
Irulan is a minor character in the Dune book.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.370
But the new movie gives her a bigger role.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:18.020
In the trailer, she says that the fall of
House Atreides is a dark secret, and she wonders

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.199
if Paul might still be alive.

00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:27.060
Cause the Harkonnens tried to kill the Atreides
secretly, to make them “die in the dark”.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:31.349
&gt;Despite the fact that the Baron promised
the Bene Gesserit that he wouldn’t kill

00:07:31.349 --> 00:07:32.979
Paul and Jessica.

00:07:32.979 --> 00:07:38.690
The Harkonnens think Paul and Jessica are
dead – they saw them fly into a storm.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:42.580
But it looks like Irulan wants to find the
truth.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:48.680
In the trailer, someone approaches a Fremen,
then we see Irulan in a.. chainmail outfit.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:52.250
Is Irulan on Arrakis, hunting for Paul?

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:57.990
That would be a big change from the book – but
as a Bene Gesserit, Irulan would have the

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:01.990
skills to infiltrate, spy and fight.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:08.189
The Dune TV adaptation on the Sci Fi Channel
also gave Irulan an investigation plotline

00:08:08.189 --> 00:08:14.840
– and gave her a similar outfit, maybe they’re
drawing inspiration here.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.500
This captured Fremen might be the character
Shishakli.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:23.670
Shishakli is a man in the book, but played
by Souheila Yacoub in the movie.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:28.220
These dead birds might have been an attempt
by Shisashakli to send a message, because

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:31.600
Fremen use birds and bats to send messages,
but maybe these soldiers stopped her.

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:35.670
We don’t know exactly what’s happening
here, but it looks like Princess Irulan has

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:40.640
a bigger role in this movie that she has in
the Dune book.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.930
Another new character is Feyd-Rautha Harkonnen,
played by Austin Butler.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:51.380
Feyd-Rautha is a nephew of the Baron Vladimir
Harkonnen, and is the brother of “Beast”

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.380
Rabban.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.980
Feyd is the Baron’s favourite nephew.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:09:01.590
Because Beast Rabban is.. a dumb brute, but
Feyd is smart, scheming, ruthless.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:08.580
In the book, Feyd-Rautha is seventeen years
old, a sullen teenager with dark hair in ringlets,

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.950
though in the new movie he’s bald.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:16.190
All the Harkonnens are bald and pale in the
Villeneuve movies, because their planet Giedi

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:24.000
Prime is ultra-industrialised, polluted, and
unnatural, so the Harkonnens are sickly, pale,

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.370
and.. &gt;bald.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:31.690
Feyd-Rautha has a sensual, effeminate quality
in the book – he has full pouting lips,

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.899
and wears tight black clothes.

00:09:33.899 --> 00:09:39.399
So in the 70s, filmmaker Jodorowsky wanted
Mick Jagger from the Rolling Stones to play

00:09:39.399 --> 00:09:40.399
Feyd.

00:09:40.399 --> 00:09:43.810
In the 80s David Lynch movie, he was played
by Sting.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:50.900
So Feyd-Rautha is like a cross between a sexy
rockstar and a psycho serial killer.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:57.550
Villeneuve says Feyd is charismatic, narcissistic,
strategic, and cruel.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:02.950
In the trailer, Feyd enters an arena, and
the curving shapes of this opening look like

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:09.680
a vulva or a mouth – Harkonnen architecture
is about consuming, swallowing everything

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:16.970
into the belly of the whale, because the Harkonnens
devour resources, people, and worlds.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:21.519
[Jodorwsky clip]
Feyd fights a gladiator in the arena, and

00:10:21.519 --> 00:10:24.670
everything’s shot in stark black and white.

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:29.140
Villeneuve said he loves the colour black,
and has long dreamed of “a world made out

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:33.260
of one color with a lot of sensuality and
high design”.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:38.750
The man who Feyd is fighting is Lieutenant
Lanville – this guy is a background character

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:44.480
in the first movie, an Atreides soldier played
by Roger Yuan, the movies’ fight coordinator.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:48.940
So it looks like Lanville was captured in
the battle in the first movie, and has now

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:53.519
been enslaved by the Harkonnens, forced to
fight for sport.

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:58.610
You can see scars on Lanville’s back – cause
the Harkonnens whip their slaves with a particular

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:05.060
vine that leaves painful scars – Gurney
has scar on his face from when he was a Harkonnen

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.060
slave.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:12.380
Also, in the background of this shot, we can
see creepy dancing figures with weirdly shaped

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.529
hats, or.. heads.

00:11:14.529 --> 00:11:19.760
So this fight scene between Feyd and Lanville
will be visually striking.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:23.390
Later, we see Feyd facing Paul.

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:28.620
Paul holds his knife to his head, which is
the same Atreides salute that Duncan used

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.399
before his death.

00:11:30.399 --> 00:11:34.410
Then Paul says “May thy knife chip and shatter”.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.740
Which is what Jamis said to Paul in the first
movie.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:43.570
So Paul learns from his Atreides teachers,
and from his Fremen teachers, and will use

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:46.440
those deadly lessons against Feyd.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.510
In seems that Paul and Feyd are destined to
clash.

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:56.200
Cause the Atreides and the Harkonnens are
opposites – the Atreides use self-control

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:02.970
to master their own minds, while the Harkonnens
are beasts ruled by their greed, lust, and

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:03.970
rage.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.410
We see Feyd roar like an animal.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:12.640
This is what Gaius talked about in the first
movie – is Paul a human, or an animal?

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:18.610
When Paul fights Feyd-Rautha, he confronts
the beast within himself.

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:23.320
So we’ll see a lot more of the Harkonnens
in Dune Part Two.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.310
This promo shot shows the Baron in a bath.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:31.050
He might still be recovering from Leto’s
poison attack in the last movie.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:36.860
Villenueve says the Baron is like a hippopotamus
cause he’s “more comfortable in liquid”

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.230
because of his weight.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:42.690
In this shot, “he’s smoking spice”,
which is wonderfully indulgent.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:51.270
The Baron is a sensualist who craves pleasure
through food and sex and every kind of physical

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:52.579
stimulation.

00:12:52.579 --> 00:12:59.459
The books don’t mention him taking baths
or smoking, but this is fitting for his personality.

00:12:59.459 --> 00:13:05.240
Another new character is Lady Margot Fenring,
played by Léa Seydoux.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:11.339
Margot watches Feyd-Rautha fight in the arena,
and the two have a closer encounter later.

00:13:11.339 --> 00:13:16.530
There’s also this shot of what might be
Margot arriving on the Harkonen planet Giedi

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:22.160
Prime – cause the surface of Giedi Prime
is full of “bitter oil” and pollution,

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:25.000
which is kinda how this black dirt looks.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:27.440
But who is Margot?

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:33.740
Margot is a Bene Gesserit, like Irulan and
Jessica, so she has powers of perception,

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.550
combat, and control.

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:42.130
She’s described in the books as “golden-haired
and willowy”, “perfection of figure”.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:47.399
Margot is married to Count Hasimir Fenring
– who might be played by Tim Blake Nelson,

00:13:47.399 --> 00:13:49.500
it’s not confirmed yet.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:54.930
But Hasimir is a politician and a friend of
the Emperor Shaddam.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:14:00.410
In the book, Hasimir and Margot worked for
the Emperor on Arrakis, smuggling spies and

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:01.529
assassins.

00:14:01.529 --> 00:14:06.050
They lived in the Arrakeen governor’s mansion
– until the Atreides moved in.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:13.779
And when the Atreides arrive, Jessica finds
a note from Margot warning her about the Harkonnens.

00:14:13.779 --> 00:14:19.520
So it seems like Margot wants to help the
Atreides, though her husband Hasimir works

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:24.380
for the Emperor, who wants to destroy the
Atreides, and the Bene Gesserit have their

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.450
own plans with Margot.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:32.860
So the Fenrings have complicated relationships
with the great powers of this universe.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:35.149
Whose side are they on?

00:14:35.149 --> 00:14:41.270
Villeneuve says Margot is a “secret agent”,
and she’s “a character full of surprises”.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:44.019
Gurney Halleck appears in the trailer.

00:14:44.019 --> 00:14:50.130
Remember, Gurney is one of Paul’s teachers,
and is one of the greatest warriors in the

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:51.130
universe.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:55.060
Last time we saw Gurney, he fought against
the Harkonnens in battle.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:59.360
And in the book, &gt;we don’t know for a while
if Gurney survives that battle.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:02.570
But the trailer shows that Gurney lives to
fight again.

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:06.759
His hair is longer now, so it looks like some
time has passed.

00:15:06.759 --> 00:15:11.449
Villeneuve says Gurney “has come back to
avenge his friends”.

00:15:11.449 --> 00:15:17.330
The trailer also shows some Fremen going through
a fancy door underground, maybe the entrance

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.910
to a sietch, a Fremen settlement.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:23.570
It’s unlocked with some kind of finger scanner.

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:27.810
In the book, Jessica opens a lock that reads
that reads the shape of her hand, so maybe

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:29.740
this is a similar technology.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:35.790
The machine also looks similar to the pain
box from the first movie – Dune often repeats

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:43.019
this imagery of facing pain, facing a test,
so that you can learn and improve yourself.

00:15:43.019 --> 00:15:49.899
So the centrepiece of the trailer is Paul
facing a deadly test – trying to ride a

00:15:49.899 --> 00:15:50.899
sandworm.

00:15:50.899 --> 00:15:56.560
In Fremen culture, riding a worm for the first
time is a coming of age ritual, this is how

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.850
a boy becomes a man.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:01.709
The phallic worm suggests sexual maturity.

00:16:01.709 --> 00:16:02.709
[show pic of Freud and Feyd-vulva].

00:16:02.709 --> 00:16:07.529
There’s also religious connotations, cause
the sandworms are like gods to the Fremen,

00:16:07.529 --> 00:16:10.959
they call them Shai-Hulud and maker.

00:16:10.959 --> 00:16:15.019
The way it works is, the Fremen plants a device
called thumper.

00:16:15.019 --> 00:16:21.070
The thumper makes a rhythmic noise which vibrates
through the ground and attracts a sandworm.

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:25.690
Then the Fremen uses these maker hooks to
climb up onto the worm.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:31.540
When they stick a hook under the sandworm’s
scales, the sandworm rolls and turns to keep

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.319
its exposed skin away from the ground.

00:16:34.319 --> 00:16:40.069
So by pulling the hooks, a Fremen can steer
the worm, and travel where they wish.

00:16:40.069 --> 00:16:45.740
But getting on top of the giant moving worm
is very dangerous, it’s easy to fall and

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:47.089
get crushed.

00:16:47.089 --> 00:16:54.010
So facing the worm is like the Old Duke facing
the bull, Leto facing the Baron, Paul facing

00:16:54.010 --> 00:17:00.060
the gom jabbar, the hunter-seeker, and Jamis
– this is a deadly test that Paul can only

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:04.380
survive through mastery of his body and mind.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:09.530
In the trailer, Stilgar tells Paul to keep
his worm ride “simple”, “Nothing fancy”,

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:11.490
just do it safely.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:14.059
Stilgar says the same thing in the book.

00:17:14.059 --> 00:17:20.089
Cause sometimes young Fremen get too excited
and proud, and they show off with tricks like

00:17:20.089 --> 00:17:23.179
dancing and doing handstands atop the worm.

00:17:23.179 --> 00:17:27.690
&gt;Paul might like to show off in front of his
crush Chani.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.460
But Stilgar doesn’t want Paul to take a
dumb risk and get killed.

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:35.070
In the trailer, Paul falls and almost dies.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.320
But he rises again, and rides the worm.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:41.340
He is now a man, a full Fremen.

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.580
And the Fremen are elated.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.380
Maybe Paul really is the messiah.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:51.170
The trailer ends with a huge crowd of Fremen
cheering Paul.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.010
It feels triumphant.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:59.320
But remember Paul’s visions in the first
movie, of the cheering crowds that bring destruction

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:06.190
– he sees “a holy war spreading across
the universe like unquenchable fire”, “A

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:08.220
war in my name!”.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:14.090
In the book, Kynes thinks that “No more
terrible disaster could befall your people

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:19.170
than for them to fall into the hands of a
Hero”.

